\\\  & =4k-17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ 4k-17 & =0 \\\\ 4k & =17 \\\\ k & =\\frac{17}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299635 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299635 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299635 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299635 #edb/ref 1069 "q-317656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299635 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299635 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $r=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $s=⟨5,1,-4⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $s$ onto $r.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{r}\\,s=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299635 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "785e36b9-0bdd-5b31-a4f6-b44338195a89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299635 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{r}\\,s & =\\frac{r\\cdot s}{r\\cdot r}r \\\\  & =\\frac{{r}_{x}{s}_{x}+{r}_{y}{s}_{y}+{r}_{z}{s}_{z}}{{r}_{x}^{2}+{r}_{y}^{2}+{r}_{z}^{2}}r \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-4)}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}}r \\\\  & =\\frac{10-1-12}{4+1+9}⟨2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{14}⟨2,-1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,-\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{3}{14},-\\frac{9}{14}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336187 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-6,-2,4⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336187 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336187 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10609a14-c18f-5c8f-8f44-594930f12d05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336221 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336221 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336221 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13bfd873-a61b-5155-b431-8c1b14ea4c36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186336351 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-2,-1,3⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921863